  "prose": [
    {
      "title": null,
      "text": "> :INFO:\n>\n> `validator-hint` class will be invisible if it comes after a `validator` class, then if the input is invalid, `validator-hint` will get visible.  \n> `validator-hint` will be visible if any previous (sibling) invalid `validator` element is present - wrap the elements (eg. in `fieldset`) to only show the hint for one invalid input.  \n> `validator-hint` still occupies space even if it's invisible because we don't want a layout shift when the hint appears.  \n> If you prefer to hide the hint when it's not visible, add `hidden` class to `validator-hint`. It will take no space when it's hidden, and if input is invalid, it will appear and take space.",
      "format": "md"
    }
  ],
